==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[baldachin]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|baldaquin|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it|en}} {{term|baldacchino|lang=it}}, from {{term|Baldacco|lang=it}}, a variant of [[Baghdad]], where the material originally came from.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbældəkɪn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{uncountable|archaic}} A kind of embroidered material with gold thread-work.
# A fine [[canopy]] of [[silk]], erected over [[shrine]]s, thrones, etc.

====Translations====
